  "stage_interpretation": {
    "issue_to_due_ms": "Configured waiting (0 for A0, exactly 2 ms for A1); not executor queueing.",
    "source_due_to_fire_ms": "Completion-source scheduling lag. Does not identify kernel scheduling versus source serialization causes.",
    "fire_to_resume_submit_ms": "Includes continuation routing before the recorded executor submission timestamp.",
    "resume_executor_wait_ms": "Submission-to-start after routing; this is not a direct kernel runq metric.",
    "zero_delay_overlap": "Original callback and resume may overlap. Source acknowledgement may follow resume execution.",
    "detached_wait": "Keeps request/drain lifetime, not executor Q/I/O.",
    "population": "Individual resume stage distributions over completed planned-request cohorts, not request critical paths or an additive p99 decomposition."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "One seed and one execution per cell; the repeated report is not a repeat experiment, confidence interval, or production p99 acceptance. The nominal top 1 percent of a 1536-request cohort contains 15.36 requests and dependencies remain.",
    "D0/A0/A1 preserve business work but intentionally alter callbacks and dependency timing. Their differences are mechanism contrasts, not identical execution contracts or pure single-operation overhead.",
    "Only home has trace1 in this pilot; trace0 O migration, load snapshots, callback timing, and source tail timing are unavailable. Home instrumentation sensitivity does not bound O instrumentation effects.",
    "CPU totals are whole-run; latency statistics are cohort-based. Helper CPU is already included in process CPU, not an additional cost to add twice.",
    "Low average helper CPU and low peak pending prove neither zero burst delays nor source scalability; home due-to-fire p99 remains about 2.6 ms.",
    "Peak inflight is retained request state, not kernel runnable threads, active workers, or sustained saturation.",
    "Quantile differences are not quantiles of paired request differences and stage quantiles cannot be added to explain request p99.",
    "Arrival lag, execution order and external environment remain potential confounders; plan provenance and hashes do not independently attest execution conditions.",
    "This controlled 50-percent, 2-ms, regular-96-QPS, 16-worker-per-cluster endpoint is not a calibrated production RPC distribution or optimal capacity/threshold choice.",
    "No Q comparison, cross-NUMA policy comparison, aligned completion burst, parent-vs-home continuation comparison, or thread-count optimization occurred in this batch."
  ],
  "next_step": {
    "scope": "Four-run A1 mechanism screen, not independent repetition acceptance; separate guide defines exact contract. Do not reopen the CPU-only matrix or infer production thresholds from this pilot."
  }
}
